# Tool-Mode Radial Menu Inventory Interaction

Source proposal: conversation analysis and suggestions of 2026-10-07.
Tracking issue: [project.todo](project.todo), Issues / Radial Menus.

## Goal and scope
    Allow configured tool-mode radial menus to coexist with hotbar and player-inventory interaction without closing merely because the player opens, focuses, clicks, or manipulates those inventories.
    Preserve engine-owned inventory operations, world-action suppression, ordinary mode-selection completion, and the chisel material-addition workflow.
    Keep tool-specific settings and context ownership in ToolModeRadialMenu; keep reusable pointer/input policy in RadialMenu.
    This document is an implementation plan. No implementation or runtime acceptance is claimed.

## Proposed assumptions and boundaries
    Defaults: enable inventory interaction for Chisel; disable it for Smithing Hammer, Boat Roller, and Generic menus. These defaults are proposed, not separately confirmed product decisions.
    Menu identity follows the nearest registered collectible base type, independently of successful specialized layout creation.
    Follow the active tool when the hotbar selection or active stack changes. Rebuild valid content; suspend selection when the active item has no usable modes, retaining the open interaction rather than applying an old mode to a different item.
    Preserve the cloned opening BlockSelection during this interaction, including chisel material additions. Opening a new interaction captures a new target.
    For a valid replacement tool, resolve that tool's configured input policy again. While suspended, retain the last resolved policy so enabled inventory navigation can continue.
    Inventory access does not change ordinary close-on-selection behavior. Preserve the existing chisel block-on-cursor keep-open exception, including its current SetToolMode semantics.
    Escape and the configured tool-mode toggle close the menu. Right-click cancels over the radial surface; inventory right-click remains available. Focus transfer between game dialogs must not cancel the radial; application focus loss still cancels it.
    Out of scope: per-collectible code/pattern overrides, a separate stay-open-after-every-selection setting, new inventory transfer algorithms, packet-format changes, layout/size redesign, and changes to quick-swap interaction behavior.
    Engine event ordering, inventory shortcut eligibility, and server packet targeting are verification prerequisites, not established runtime facts.

## Source map
    Shared menu boundary: ../VanillaExpanded/src/RadialMenu/IRadialMenu.cs and RadialMenuSystem.cs.
    Pointer/keyboard capture and cancellation: ../VanillaExpanded/src/RadialMenu/RadialMenuDialog.cs.
    Hover, selection, and KeepOpen state: ../VanillaExpanded/src/RadialMenu/RadialMenuInteraction.cs.
    Tool-mode owner and captured context: ../VanillaExpanded/src/ToolModeRadialMenu/ToolModeRadialMenuSystem.cs.
    Collectible layout resolution: ../VanillaExpanded/src/ToolModeRadialMenu/ToolModeMenuLayoutStrategyRegistry.cs.
    Content and mode-index conversion: ../VanillaExpanded/src/ToolModeRadialMenu/ToolModeMenuContentFactory.cs.
    Client mutation and server packet: ../VanillaExpanded/src/ToolModeRadialMenu/ToolModeSelection.cs.
    Existing configuration: ../VanillaExpanded/src/VanillaExpandedConfig.cs, ../VanillaExpanded/assets/vanillaexpanded/config/configlib-patches.json, and localized assets.
    Existing focused tests: ../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/ToolModeRadialMenu and ../VanillaExpanded.Tests/RadialMenu.
    Engine reference sources: ../../vsapi/Client/UI/Dialog/GuiDialog.cs and ../../vssurvivalmod/Item/ItemChisel.cs, relative to this document. Inspect installed VintagestoryLib/server code for dispatch details absent from these source repositories.

## Phase 1: Establish engine routing and selection contracts
    Outcome: a concrete routing contract and target-validation rules that later work can implement safely.
    ☐ Inspect installed engine GUI dispatch for raw mouse capture, Handled propagation, InputOrder, focus requests, hotkey routing, Escape routing, and inventory opening/closing.
        ☐ Determine whether an inventory opening or focus request closes competing dialogs, and identify the narrow integration needed if it does.
        ☐ Establish how inventory slot hits, dialog bounds, foreground dialogs, and wheel events are recognized through existing APIs.
        ☐ Specify overlap precedence consistent with visible drawing: visible radial surface owns radial input; foreground engine dialogs retain their input; covered inventory slots cannot receive clicks through the radial.
        ☐ Specify how allowed inventory events reach the normal engine dispatcher while unclaimed world-space events remain suppressed, including right-click and rebound mouse controls.
        ☐ Identify inventory-toggle and hotbar-selection hotkeys through registered engine hotkeys rather than hard-coded key numbers; specify matching key-down/key-up ownership and inventory modifier shortcuts.
    ☐ Inspect the installed server handler for ToolMode packet 27 and its held-item/active-slot authority.
        ☐ Verify required ordering between inventory/hotbar synchronization and mode packets, including rapid slot changes and material pickup.
        ☐ Define validity checks for the active slot, stack identity, collectible, opening block target, and selected mode index before mutation or packet transmission.
        ☐ Define target invalidation: missing/replaced chisel block or unusable modes suspends selection; no packet may use stale content.
    ☐ Review these findings against the proposed assumptions above and record concrete decisions here before enabling input passthrough.
    Completion criteria:
        ☐ Engine GUI/world routing and authoritative mode targeting have source or installed-assembly evidence.
        ☐ Pointer ownership, overlap precedence, permitted keys, suspension, and target invalidation have implementable contracts.

## Phase 2: Add profile settings and reusable interaction policy
    Depends on Phase 1.
    Outcome: each tool-mode profile can request inventory interaction without coupling the shared menu to tool types.
    ☐ Add client configuration booleans for Chisel, Smithing Hammer, Boat Roller, and Generic inventory interaction in VanillaExpandedConfig.
        ☐ Use explicit defaults from the assumptions; omitted fields in older configurations retain those defaults.
        ☐ Add ConfigLib controls, translated labels/tooltips, and visible grouping under Radial Menus.
    ☐ Resolve profile identity and configuration in ToolModeRadialMenu using nearest-base-type matching.
        ☐ Reuse the existing collectible type-resolution contract; avoid duplicating a second drifting type map or embedding input policy in geometry strategies.
        ☐ Test derived collectibles, unregistered generic tools, and specialized-layout fallback without losing the collectible's profile.
    ☐ Extend IRadialMenu/Open and its dialog/system implementation with an explicit generic interaction option.
        ☐ Preserve the existing Open signature/default contract for quick-swap and other existing callers.
        ☐ Define the narrow update needed for policy changes during an open interaction; reset policy and input ownership on close or failed open.
        ☐ Keep composition roots thin; each new source file owns one named responsibility. Document new methods/classes and nontrivial logic, and group methods by visibility and functional family.
    ☐ Add focused configuration/default/profile tests and compatibility checks for existing menu callers.
    Completion criteria:
        ☐ Per-profile settings serialize and appear in the existing client configuration UI.
        ☐ Generic radial APIs contain no collectible-specific policy, and existing callers retain their prior behavior.

## Phase 3: Maintain a valid tool-mode interaction context
    Depends on Phases 1 and 2; complete before enabling inventory input in Phase 4.
    Outcome: an open menu follows active-tool changes and cannot select stale mode content.
    ☐ Replace captured opening slot/collectible callback assumptions with an owned interaction context in ToolModeRadialMenu.
        ☐ Keep the cloned opening block target and resolve the current active slot/stack for each valid context.
        ☐ Observe active-slot/stack changes through verified engine events; use a bounded open-session check only where an event contract is missing.
        ☐ Refresh layout, entries, selected-mode presentation, and profile policy when their context changes; do not rebuild unchanged geometry every frame.
        ☐ Suspend selection for empty slots, missing modes, or invalid targets. Present a localized explanation without exposing implementation details.
        ☐ Resume and rebuild when a usable active tool/target context returns, without reopening the dialog.
    ☐ Validate the current context immediately before ToolModeSelection.Apply.
        ☐ Reject selections from obsolete content generations, including a mouse gesture begun before a tool/layout change.
        ☐ Refresh or suspend on rejection without applying client mutation or sending a mode packet.
        ☐ Retain engine-owned inventory synchronization and the existing authoritative packet format.
    ☐ Preserve chisel behavior: read MouseItemSlot at selection time, apply existing material semantics, keep open for block-on-cursor operations, and refresh material entries.
        ☐ Handle unsuccessful material additions and delayed authoritative updates without showing stale selectable indices.
    ☐ Apply live configuration changes through ILiveConfigurable without closing solely to change inventory permission; reset outstanding gestures when policy changes.
        ☐ Feature disablement still cancels. Dispose/world exit release any added subscriptions or callbacks exactly once.
    ☐ Add focused tests for active-slot changes, replacement by another stack of the same collectible, empty/no-mode suspension, resume, invalid target, obsolete gestures, and no packet on invalid selection.
    Completion criteria:
        ☐ Local mutation and packet creation use one validated current context.
        ☐ Tool/content changes and suspension never leave old mode entries actionable.

## Phase 4: Route inventory input without relinquishing world-action protection
    Depends on Phase 3.
    Outcome: enabled menus allow normal inventory interactions while remaining open.
    ☐ Implement the verified routing contract in RadialMenuDialog and narrowly scoped input helpers.
        ☐ Update CaptureAllInputs/CaptureRawMouse and individual handlers consistently; changing capture flags alone is insufficient.
        ☐ Preserve already-handled events and let engine inventory dialogs process permitted events through their normal paths; do not manually move stacks or synthesize duplicate inventory clicks.
        ☐ Share rendered geometry with radial surface hit-testing, including disabled entries, center, and separators. Clear radial hover when input belongs to an inventory/foreground dialog.
        ☐ Track per-button press ownership across move/up events. Inventory gestures cannot select radial entries; radial gestures cannot leak releases into inventory or world input.
        ☐ Cancel radial selection when its release leaves the valid radial surface or its context generation changes.
        ☐ Permit right-click stack splitting over inventory; cancel only for radial-owned right-clicks in enabled mode.
        ☐ Route wheel events according to the receiving inventory/hotbar contract; consume them over the radial and suppress unintended world actions.
        ☐ Allow verified inventory-toggle, hotbar-selection, and inventory shortcut keys while retaining suppression of unrelated gameplay actions. Respect configured keybindings and focused inventory text controls.
        ☐ Keep Escape/tool-mode-toggle and application-focus-loss cancellation deterministic; ordinary GUI focus transfer must leave the menu open.
        ☐ Suppress both left/right in-world actions, including input held before opening and rebound controls, using established engine mechanisms.
    ☐ Preserve restrictive routing for profiles with the setting disabled and for existing quick-swap callers.
    ☐ Add meaningful routing/gesture tests covering disabled entries, separators, overlaps, cross-boundary drags, key-up pairing, policy changes mid-gesture, and world-action suppression.
    Completion criteria:
        ☐ Permitted inventory events are delivered once; radial selection is delivered only for a valid radial gesture.
        ☐ Enabled inventory interaction does not close the menu, and non-GUI world actions remain suppressed.

## Phase 5: Validate, review, and document acceptance
    Depends on Phase 4.
    Outcome: focused evidence and user-run runtime acceptance establish the complete interaction contract.
    ☐ Use subagents for all build/test tool execution, as required by repository instructions.
        ☐ Run focused RadialMenu, ToolModeRadialMenu, and configuration tests, then the appropriate Release build.
        ☐ If shared compilation causes output contention, use isolated outputs with UseSharedCompilation=false.
        ☐ Verify shipped configuration/localization assets through the established packaging workflow.
    ☐ Obtain user-run in-game checks; do not launch the game for visual acceptance.
        ☐ Open the chisel radial, open/close player inventory, pick up material from inventory/hotbar, click Add Material repeatedly, and return the remainder to inventory without incidental menu closure.
        ☐ Verify right-click splitting, modifier transfers, inventory scrolling, hotbar number/wheel selection, and remapped inventory/tool-mode keys.
        ☐ Verify empty/no-mode suspension and resume, same-collectible stack replacement, rapid tool switching, and invalidated block targets.
        ☐ Verify inventory/radial overlap, cursor-held stack visibility, Escape and toggle behavior, and no world action from either mouse button or cross-boundary gestures.
        ☐ Check chisel material synchronization with a multiplayer server; distinguish this receipt from singleplayer and headless tests.
        ☐ Verify each disabled profile, quick-swap, ordinary mode-selection close behavior, config reload, application focus loss, pause, and world exit.
    ☐ Perform a second implementation review and an independent completion audit against this full document before checking completion markers.
    ☐ Add concise user-facing setting/workflow documentation and remove temporary diagnostic logging.
    ☐ Update the linked project.todo issue only after all required evidence is present; record any unverified runtime checks here as remaining work.
    Completion criteria:
        ☐ Focused tests, Release build, asset packaging, second review, and independent audit have fresh receipts.
        ☐ User-run GUI and multiplayer checks are recorded separately from automated evidence.
        ☐ Every task is satisfied or explicitly remains unchecked with its limitation stated; no headless result is treated as visual/runtime acceptance.
